~ start
Marley Mildred: Captain, let's make this snappy no? John betrayed you because he's sad you killed his friends. End of story.
John S. Hark: I might not agree with you Captain, but I'm not ready to raise a mutiny. I think Marley waited until the other leaders of the crew were gone. That way he'd have no opposition.
Marley Mildred: Why believe him? 
John S. Hark: He's more likely to believe me than believe you.
Marley Mildred: Well Captain, what be your choice?
=> END